ndRunning`, `AiOff`; every mapping's tests in `ipc_error/tests.rs`), `frontend_log.rs` (`LogEntry` → `tracing`, target `frontend`), `mock_window.rs` (tests only: a conflict or operation repository opened in a mock-runtime window, `invoke` a command by name, `invoke_on` from another thread, `ending()` calls `outcome::ending_when_git_is_done` — the close ending as `window.rs` computes it; used by the command tests in `commands.rs`, `merge/tests.rs` and `servers.rs`; `open_compare_window`: the compare window on a temp data folder, used by `compare.rs`; `range.rs` builds its own mock window over a `diverged_repo` and calls `invoke_on`). Merge window: `Mutex<Merge>` and `Mutex<Host>`; compare window: `Mutex<TabStore>`; range window: `Mutex<ThreadStore>`, the send guard `Mutex<()>` and `Mutex<AiState>` (held by a prepare while git makes the checkout, and by the start's sweep). Never two held together, but for a send: it holds the send guard throughout and takes `threads` only between glab calls; a command locks one, calls one method and lets go; a worker never holds the merge's lock while git runs, nor the store's while it diffs, nor the AI's while it looks at the checkout. `bin/export-bindings.rs` generates `frontend/src/ipc/bindings.ts` (`just bindings`). `tauri.conf.json` `bundle.resources` ships `LICENSE` and `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.txt` (`scripts/third-party-licenses.sh`) in every bundle. Depends on `session`, `settings`, `lsp-host`, `compare`, `range`, `review` and `agent` only, never on `gitio` or `merge-core` (arch-check).
